From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:18:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] thermal: add the OnePlus Pad 4 shell temperature estimate
 (stock Horae model)

The stock thermal daemon of the OnePlus Pad 4 (Horae) estimates the shell
temperature of each surface with a linear model of a few board sensors
over the present sample and the three before it, five seconds apart,
plus a constant, and takes the hottest surface; until a model has its
history, the battery temperature plus a bias stands in. Our userspace
iceland-thermal implements that model from the decoded stock
configuration (iceland-firmware thermal-model.json). Add the same
estimate as a read-only, tripless thermal zone "horae-shell", so the
thermal core and tools can read it next to the daemon's value.

The models come from the device tree (child nodes: zone-names,
coefficients-micro, constant-micro-celsius); the battery may be a thermal
zone or the power supply. The sensor is not bound by default: only the
opt-in device tree describes it.

The idea of an in-kernel Horae estimator comes from SuperTurtleDev's
oplus_shell_temp.c (iceland-mainline-kernel-linux f3e9d0fe7ac7, posted
without a Signed-off-by); this driver is a separate implementation, no
code was copied.

Based-on: SuperTurtleDev iceland-mainline-kernel-linux f3e9d0fe7ac7, oplus_shell_temp.c (idea only)
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/thermal/Kconfig               |  12 +
 drivers/thermal/Makefile              |   1 +
 drivers/thermal/iceland_horae_shell.c | 306 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 319 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/thermal/iceland_horae_shell.c

